WWII, but like many other Japanese aircraft it lacked armor which made it vulnerable in combat against Allied fighters. The D4Y was produced from 1942 to 1945 with 2,038 aircraft manufactured in total, including many variants.","LocalizedString":"The Yokosuka D4Y Suisei (e. comet) was a Japanese two seated, carrier-based dive bomber used during WWII by the Imperial Japanese Navy. The D4Y came into service in 1942, and although it was initially designed as a dive bomber, it also served as a night fighter, reconnaissance aircraft and lastly it was used for kamikaze attacks. The D4Y was the fastest dive bomber of WWII, but like many other Japanese aircraft it lacked armor which made it vulnerable in combat against Allied fighters. The D4Y was produced from 1942 to 1945 with 2,038 aircraft manufactured in total, including many variants."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Expansion2019","isReserved":true,"hasDeployment":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion_Small'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Explosion_Small.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/t_d4y_judy.t_d4y_judy","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Darryl Legg","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/D4Y_SUISEI.D4Y_SUISEI","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":290.0},"historyPhotoSource":" http://www.ijnafpics.com/JB&W3/D4Y3-9.jpg","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_d4y_suisei_photo","SourceString":"A Yokosuka D4Y3 Type 33 Suisei in flight.","LocalizedString":"A Yokosuka D4Y3 Type 33 Suisei in flight."},"historyTypeDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_d4y_suisei_header","SourceString":"Dive Bomber","LocalizedString":"Dive Bomber"},"blowUpExplosion":{"ObjectName":"ParticleSystem'P_ExplosionAircraftS'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Explosions/Small/Aircraft/P_ExplosionAircraftS.119"}